\section{The tiered lookup}

[[find_preprint]] tries the link sources from most to least
trustworthy and returns the first adoptable result.  The recorded-link
tier comes first because version-aware deduplication
(\cref{sec:version-dedup}) may already have seen the preprint in the
same result set and stored it in [[preprint_versions]]---discarding
that in-hand link only to rediscover it over the network (or worse,
fail to) would be absurd.  The two authoritative tiers need the
published DOI, so they are skipped for DOI-less papers; the search
tier works from title and authors alone.

Each tier is wrapped in a broad exception guard rather than trusting
the clients' own silent-failure contracts: a bug in one tier must
degrade to \enquote{no preprint found}, never break enrichment---the
same reasoning the providers apply to their own network errors.

<<preprint lookup functions>>=
def find_preprint(paper: Paper, search: bool = False) -> Paper | None:
    """Find an adoptable preprint version of `paper`.

    Tries, in order: preprint links recorded on the paper, OpenAlex's
    alternate locations of the published DOI, Crossref's
    `has-preprint` relation, and---only when `search` is true---a
    title+author search over preprint servers.

    Returns a replacement entry (the preprint, with the published DOI
    recorded in `published_versions`), the same entry with just the
    PDF filled in when the preprint copy has no DOI of its own, or
    None when no preprint with a PDF is found. Returns None when the
    paper already has a PDF.
    """
    if paper.pdf_url:
        return None

    finders = [_from_recorded_versions]
    if paper.doi:
        finders.append(_from_openalex_locations)
        finders.append(_from_crossref_relation)
    if search:
        finders.append(_from_title_search)

    for finder in finders:
        try:
            replacement = finder(paper)
        except Exception as e:
            logger.debug("preprint: tier %r failed: %s", finder, e)
            continue
        if replacement is not None:
            return replacement
    return None
@

