\section{Adopting a candidate}

All tiers funnel through one decision: is this candidate an adoptable
preprint, and what does the replacement entry look like?  Centralizing
it keeps the adoption rules identical across tiers.

The rules, and why each exists:
\begin{description}
\item[Reject the published work itself] A lookup can echo the very
  DOI we started from (OpenAlex serves merged works under either
  DOI).  Comparing normalized DOIs catches that; adopting it would
  discard the entry's identity for nothing.
\item[Adopt only with a PDF] The candidate's own record may lack a
  PDF link, so we give Unpaywall a chance to fill it from the
  \emph{preprint's} DOI before giving up.  If there is still no PDF,
  there is nothing to gain from the swap.
\item[Carry over content the preprint lacks] Preprint-server records
  are often sparser than publisher records.  The work's content
  metadata---authors, year, abstract, keywords, tags---transfers
  between versions just as in [[merge_version_of]]
  (\cref{sec:version-merge}), filling only gaps, and provenance
  sources are unioned.
\item[Record the provenance link] The published DOI lands in
  [[published_versions]], which marks the entry as a deliberate
  substitution ([[is_preprint_substitute]]): the verify report shows
  it as \enquote{preprint of \dots} rather than a stale entry, and
  session merges recognize the published version as already present.
  Any [[preprint_versions]] link is cleared---the entry now \emph{is}
  the preprint.
\end{description}

<<preprint lookup functions>>=
def _adopt(published: Paper, candidate: Paper | None) -> Paper | None:
    """Build the replacement entry for an adoptable candidate."""
    if candidate is None:
        return None
    if (
        candidate.doi
        and published.doi
        and Paper._normalize_doi(candidate.doi)
        == Paper._normalize_doi(published.doi)
    ):
        return None

    if not candidate.pdf_url:
        candidate = unpaywall.annotate_paper(candidate)
    if not candidate.pdf_url:
        return None

    combined_sources = list(candidate.sources)
    for src in published.sources:
        if src not in combined_sources:
            combined_sources.append(src)

    published_versions = list(candidate.published_versions or [])
    if published.doi and not any(
        entry.get("doi") == published.doi
        for entry in published_versions
    ):
        published_versions.append(
            {"doi": published.doi, "relation": "preprint-of"}
        )

    return replace(
        candidate,
        authors=(
            candidate.authors
            if candidate.authors
            else list(published.authors)
        ),
        year=(
            candidate.year
            if candidate.year is not None
            else published.year
        ),
        abstract=candidate.abstract or published.abstract,
        keywords=Paper._merge_term_lists(
            candidate.keywords, published.keywords
        ),
        tags=Paper._merge_term_lists(candidate.tags, published.tags),
        sources=combined_sources,
        preprint_versions=None,
        published_versions=published_versions or None,
    )
@

