\section{Tier 0: links recorded by deduplication}

When a search returned both versions of a work, the version-aware
dedup pass (\cref{sec:version-dedup}) collapsed them onto the
published entry and left the preprint's DOI and PDF URL in
[[preprint_versions]].  This tier redeems those links.  When the link
has a DOI we resolve it through the OpenAlex DOI lookup to recover the
full preprint record (venue, URL, abstract); if that fails---or the
link never had a DOI---we fall back to a minimal candidate built from
the published entry's own content plus the link's data, which is
enough for [[_adopt]] to work with.

<<preprint lookup functions>>=
def _from_recorded_versions(paper: Paper) -> Paper | None:
    """Adopt a preprint link recorded in `paper.preprint_versions`."""
    for link in paper.preprint_versions or []:
        doi = link.get("doi")
        pdf_url = link.get("pdf_url")
        if not doi and not pdf_url:
            continue

        candidate = None
        if doi:
            provider = get_provider("openalex")
            if provider is not None:
                candidate = provider.get_paper_by_doi(doi)
        if candidate is None:
            candidate = Paper(
                title=paper.title,
                authors=list(paper.authors),
                year=paper.year,
                doi=doi,
                abstract=paper.abstract,
                pdf_url=pdf_url,
                sources=list(paper.sources),
            )
        elif not candidate.pdf_url and pdf_url:
            candidate = replace(candidate, pdf_url=pdf_url)

        adopted = _adopt(paper, candidate)
        if adopted is not None:
            return adopted
    return None
@

