\section{Tier 1: OpenAlex locations}

OpenAlex often merges a preprint deposit into the same work as the
published version, so the published DOI's own record already lists the
preprint host in its [[locations]] array
(\cref{sec:openalex}).  The subtlety is identity: a location
is a \emph{copy}, not a record, and carries no DOI of its own.  For
arXiv locations we can derive the canonical arXiv DOI from the URL
([[arxiv_doi_from_url]], \cref{utils-module}) and adopt a full
replacement.  For other hosts there is nothing citable to swap to, so
we keep the entry's identity and only fill in the PDF---the reader
gets the preprint's file, and the citation stays with the published
version, which in this case is the only version we can address.

<<preprint lookup functions>>=
def _from_openalex_locations(paper: Paper) -> Paper | None:
    """Adopt a preprint location of the published DOI's own work."""
    provider = get_provider("openalex")
    if provider is None:
        return None

    for location in provider.get_preprint_locations(paper.doi):
        pdf_url = location.get("pdf_url")
        if not pdf_url:
            continue

        candidate_doi = arxiv_doi_from_url(pdf_url) or arxiv_doi_from_url(
            location.get("landing_page_url")
        )
        if candidate_doi:
            candidate = provider.get_paper_by_doi(candidate_doi)
            if candidate is None:
                candidate = Paper(
                    title=paper.title,
                    authors=list(paper.authors),
                    year=paper.year,
                    doi=candidate_doi,
                    venue=location.get("source_name"),
                    pdf_url=pdf_url,
                    sources=list(paper.sources),
                )
            elif not candidate.pdf_url:
                candidate = replace(candidate, pdf_url=pdf_url)
            adopted = _adopt(paper, candidate)
            if adopted is not None:
                return adopted
        else:
            return replace(paper, pdf_url=pdf_url)
    return None
