\section{Tier 2: Crossref's has-preprint relation}

Crossref's [[has-preprint]] relation is the publisher's own assertion
that a preprint exists, DOI to DOI (\cref{crossref-module}).  Coverage
is sparse---many publishers never deposit it---but when present it is
the strongest possible link and costs nothing beyond the currency
lookup enrichment already makes.  We resolve the preprint DOI to a
full record through OpenAlex where possible; failing that, a minimal
candidate with the preprint DOI still lets [[_adopt]] try Unpaywall
for the PDF.

<<preprint lookup functions>>=
def _from_crossref_relation(paper: Paper) -> Paper | None:
    """Adopt a preprint named by Crossref's `has-preprint` relation."""
    provider = get_provider("openalex")
    for doi in crossref.fetch_preprint_dois(paper.doi):
        candidate = None
        if provider is not None:
            candidate = provider.get_paper_by_doi(doi)
        if candidate is None:
            candidate = Paper(
                title=paper.title,
                authors=list(paper.authors),
                year=paper.year,
                doi=doi,
                abstract=paper.abstract,
                sources=list(paper.sources),
            )
        adopted = _adopt(paper, candidate)
        if adopted is not None:
            return adopted
    return None
@

