\section{Tier 3: title+author search}

The last resort searches for the work by title and accepts only
candidates whose [[legacy_hash_paper_id]] equals the paper's own---the
strict rule from the design overview.  Two queries cover all servers:
one type-filtered OpenAlex search spans the seven OpenAlex-hosted
servers plus OpenAlex's arXiv and HAL indexing
(\cref{sec:openalex}), and one native arXiv search covers the
most common case with fresher data than OpenAlex's index.  We
deliberately do not fan out to all nine providers of the
[[preprints]] group; that would multiply request cost for no extra
coverage.

The identity check compares hashes of \emph{candidate} title and
authors against the published entry's, so a candidate with no authors
(some OpenAlex preprint records are sparse) hashes differently and is
rejected---conservative, as a match on title alone is exactly the
false-positive risk this tier must avoid.  [[_adopt]] then rejects
candidates that turn out to be the published record itself.

The arXiv query is scoped to the title field ([[ti:"..."]]) rather
than sent as a general relevance query.  arXiv's relevance ranking is
weak for titles made of common words---a general query for
\enquote{Attention Is All You Need} does not return that paper in its
top hits---while the title-field search puts the exact-title match
first, which is the only kind of hit our matcher can accept anyway.
Embedded quotes are stripped so the title cannot break out of the
quoted field expression.

<<preprint lookup functions>>=
def _from_title_search(paper: Paper) -> Paper | None:
    """Adopt a preprint found by strict title+author search."""
    if not paper.title or not paper.title.strip():
        return None

    target = legacy_hash_paper_id(paper.title, paper.authors)

    candidates: list[Paper] = []
    openalex = get_provider("openalex")
    if openalex is not None:
        candidates.extend(
            openalex.search_preprints_by_title(paper.title)
        )
    arxiv = get_provider("arxiv")
    if arxiv is not None and arxiv.is_available():
        quoted = paper.title.strip().replace('"', " ")
        candidates.extend(arxiv.search(f'ti:"{quoted}"', limit=5))

    for candidate in candidates:
        if (
            legacy_hash_paper_id(candidate.title, candidate.authors)
            != target
        ):
            continue
        adopted = _adopt(paper, candidate)
        if adopted is not None:
            return adopted
    return None
@

